e  seemed to hold across them  the fact that alaka has largely not been  there tells you how hands-off all the  other characters have been towards her  and how afraid they've potentially been  about invoking something or bringing  something into the room  and that's the first actively  interesting thing to me this arc  it's also the thing that explained why  it's so important that kilwa  specifically is there for alaka  and that kiwa plans to be with alaka  forever one thing i didn't understand  about this episode was subone's  musings on kilwa subuni thinking keel  wise heartless and cruel is an  observation i wouldn't have made based  on what i've seen of him  and i wonder whether it was born of the  fact that he plans to make sure  something stays asleep and alaka gets to  live or the fact that he's got his own  brand of toxicity that's about to come  in  once he's made this wish for gone and i  suppose there's no way to know that yet  because the story needs to progress a  little bit more to get to it but making  the observation that when he was being  controlled he suffered less suggests  that the heartlessness and cruelty he's  showing is to himself that being  controlled there was greater  self-preservation and maybe that's  really what it is  in a family of assassins catching  feelings of any kind is going to limit  the quality or effectiveness or  willingness to do your job  and maybe that's what subuni's seeing  more than anything there's so much to  consider with the little murder boy and  i suspect i'll be thinking of him for  some time  artistically before i move on to the  next episode there were some beautiful  choices made  the romance of tension and held moments  for leorio despite  us knowing it's gone the images of  everyone around him and the clear and  open  beauty of leorio's feelings toward the  kid were heartwarming to say the least  anyway moving on to episode 146 as  predicted  episode 146 was a doozy a familial doozy  no less  turns out i 